# promise: #495
# A two-finger swipe back over a Little Window's page with nothing behind it closes the window, as
# in Arc (a swipe goes where Back goes, WebContentsUIDelegate::CanExternallyNavigate), and Back
# (⌘[) does the same. A test can't make the gesture, so cra://debug?littleSwipeBack= asks the
# newest Little Window's page delegate what Chromium's swipe asks before it starts (go=1: the end).
budget rss=700 stalls50=20
pace 0.5
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "defaultLinkDestination": {"littleWindow": {}}}
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=main
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)

# A link from another app opens in a Little Window, on its first page: the swipe may start, and
# its end closes the window.
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=little
wait 3
cra://debug?littleShown=open
expect-log little shown open: windows=1
cra://debug?littleSwipeBack=first&go=1
expect-log little swipe back first: can=1$
wait 1.5
cra://debug?littleShown=swiped
expect-log little shown swiped: windows=0

# Back (⌘[) on a Little Window's first page closes it too.
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=again
wait 3
cra://debug?littleShown=again
expect-log little shown again: windows=1
cra://action/goBack
wait 1.5
cra://debug?littleShown=back
expect-log little shown back: windows=0
